[5] Proof readout
  1. S194 leaves 15 route-mixed coarse ET+unit fibers, but all 38
     packets are strict-open; this pass only schedules certificates.
  2. Topology alone contracts the 15 mixed fibers to 3 mixed topology
     classes, but a common open-topology class still mixes routes.
  3. Unit-scale alone separates nonunit covering rows from most direct
     q-witness rows, but unit-scale covering rows still mix with
     unit q-witness rows.
  4. Joining topology compact signature with the unit-scale tooth gives
     21 residual fibers and 0 route-mixed fibers.
  5. The compressed topology bucket joined to the same unit-scale tooth
     gives the same purity on the stored S194 residual ledger.
